# Line endings are LF everywhere — in the index and in the working tree.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Git for Windows default, so without this file a checkout (or a stash pop) rewrites every
# text file with CRLF while the index keeps LF. Two static tests read files byte for byte — `claude-md-commands`
# compares the command list in CLAUDE.md, and the design-system test matches the `@supports` blocks in globals.css —
# so they failed on Windows for a reason no diff could show [observed 2026-09-23, after a stash cycle reverted the
# tree]. The app also ships text to a thermal printer, where a stray CR is a real byte on a real receipt.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit and checks out LF regardless of `core.autocrlf`.
* text=auto eol=lf

